\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {15}{\ignorespaces Topology at matched agent count (Llama 3.3 70B, $n = 7$ agents, no defence, 40 natural runs, 30 controlled trials per edge, fixed-artefact protocol throughout). The three topologies have similar mean per-hop survival but differ substantially in outcome. The star--tree ASR gap is within noise at this size ($p = 0.60$); the chain--tree and chain--star gaps survive the family-wise control of Appendix\nonbreakingspace \ref {app:mult}, so the ``most permissive'' ordering is numerical only. $R_0$ is reported without an interval: its numerator and denominator are formed per agent-instance and are not recoverable from the per-cell files we archived, so the interval we would have to print would not be reproducible from the release.}}{9}{table.caption.40}\protected@file@percent }
